(charger) rather than always resolving cleanly. This also answers \"it should feel like me\" directly, since it's not a borrowed case-study template.\n\n## The two-minute reader\n\nYou told me who this is for, and it changes the pacing more than anything else. A placement reviewer isn't going to sit through a slow scroll-story to find your CV. So:\n\n- The hero carries everything essential on load, with no animation gating it: name, course, stage, \"looking for a summer 2026 placement,\" CV download, email — all visible before any scroll happens.\n- A CV/contact affordance stays reachable throughout (small persistent corner element), not just at the very end.\n- The exploded-view scroll-story is for the reader who stays past the first screen — it's depth, not a prerequisite. Keep each scroll-beat short; nobody should need more than a few seconds per section to get the point even without reading the prose.\n\n## Assumptions I'm making (flag if wrong)\n\n- Using the job-card format for Formula Student and the charger, even though those aren't literally job cards — reusing your real format, not fabricating a new one.\n- Co-op section states tenure only, no count, unless you later pull a real number from the job cards (optional, not needed to build).\n- No photo of you required — can add later if you want one.\n- Slow Miles section stays photo-led (garage-floor inventory, strip-down shots) since that material already exists and needs no embellishment.\n\nEverything else from the first plan (colour/type, mobile fallback, section order, what to gather) stands as before. Let me know if this is right, or if the job-card format should take over more of the site than just those three sections before we move to building."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5042,"cache_read_input_tokens":18147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5042},"outp